body:
I am also getting this error after having the application run for about 2 months

```bash
WARN  [nioEventLoopGroup-2-1] DefaultChannelPipeline: An exceptionCaught() event was fired, and it reached at the tail of the pipeline. It usually means the last handler in the pipeline did not handle the exception.
java.io.IOException: Too many open files
        at sun.nio.ch.ServerSocketChannelImpl.accept0(Native Method)
        at sun.nio.ch.ServerSocketChannelImpl.accept(ServerSocketChannelImpl.java:422)
        at sun.nio.ch.ServerSocketChannelImpl.accept(ServerSocketChannelImpl.java:250)
        at io.netty.util.internal.SocketUtils$5.run(SocketUtils.java:110)

```

How do I prevent the application from opening multiple connections that don't close?

Below are the relevant parts of the code that is running:

```java
public class TcpServerHandler extends SimpleChannelInboundHandler<ByteBuf> {
	
	@Override
	public void channelRead0(ChannelHandlerContext ctx, ByteBuf buf) throws Exception {
		// ReferenceCountUtil.release is called by SimpleChannelInboundHandler
		// ...
		ChannelFuture cf = ctx.writeAndFlush(Unpooled.copiedBuffer(new byte[] { 0x06 }));
		if (!cf.isSuccess())
			log.error("Sending acknowledgement failed with root cause", cf.cause());
		} else
			log.warn("Nothing happened");
	}
}
```

I don't think `ulimit` is the solution here as some resources are not freed up. I only get this error after the application has run for a few months, after which I have to restart it.

My configuration settings are:

```properties
SO_BACKLOG=100
BOSS_GROUP_THREADS=2
WORKER_GROUP_THREADS=2
```
